../../../docs/context/decision_log.md:530:- **Decision (Apurva):** the case page continues the blue-tint theme with a **compact** task header: brand-subtle tinted, sticky, holding **Back** (per D-48 stage), the **patient's name** (20/28 semibold, `.tm-text-h1`), age/gender and the case number underneath, and **Help** on the right. No logo, no profile button. Content scrolls on white with its cards.
../../../docs/context/decision_log.md:555:- **Why:** "Confirm Order" names the customer's order, not the doctor's act; the act is issuing the prescription (D-36 counts a case as done at that point). "Confirm the case" was considered and rejected — vague, reads like accepting the case.
