../../../docs/context/decision_log.md:778:  1. **Profile opens as a page**, not a bottom sheet: task header with Back and the title "Profile" (no logo); grey page with white cards at the 16 margin — name and role · Today's earnings · User manual and Faster sign-in rows · **Log out last in the content** (not pinned: not the page's main action; fewer accidental taps). Open case → the "You can log out after this case is closed." note. **Log out? stays a sheet** (confirmations are sheets). Scales to Help, settings, earnings history later.
../../../docs/context/decision_log.md:789:  1. **One case page file**, not two. The **calling markup is the approved one** (D-58 points 16, 17, 21): the live-call card is titled **"End-of-call script"** and the label inside the script box is hidden. The entry-pass "Call" heading is a leftover from before D-58.
../../../docs/context/decision_log.md:791:  3. **The 8px offset is a leftover 24px margin** in one of the two stylesheets; **16 is correct** (D-67). Fix the leftover, don't keep both.
../../../docs/context/decision_log.md:810:  4. **Promotion close-out:** guard 5.12 fixed in the design system, not as exceptions — `.tm-header-task--compact` follows the 16 page margin (D-67) and `.tm-notice--question` is the 7b question (D-62 pt 2); the case page drops its local overrides. Profile: the promoted code is the approved look (D-70 page); pictures re-baselined. Sheet labels typed in code are accepted for now (rebuild item; the error lines are already in the registry). Log out has no icon (D-70). `home/availability.html` and `home/add-availability.html` are retired — `home.html` covers the same states; NATIVE-HANDOFF points there. Captures use a fixed clock date so pictures don't change daily.
../../../docs/context/decision_log.md:854:  2. **Release is not Hold.** Release = "not me", the case goes back to the queue; Patient unavailable = today's 216 ORDER ON HOLD (automatic on a failed call, by hand only in 7d); Callback = talk later. All three kept, one job each. Ops tracks the release rate per doctor (misuse to skip hard cases), as with Unavailable (D-73).
../../../docs/context/decision_log.md:855:  3. **SOS limit prints the daily total in the medicine's unit (P-01):** "2 puffs as needed (max 8 puffs/day)" (dose × max doses); cream "Apply as needed (max 3 times/day)". The doctor still enters dose and Max doses a day. Same for SOS only and "+ SOS". Changes D-16's printed format. The PRD carries the full medicine-type table (form · unit · dose options · printed-line examples), after P-02 / P-03 are settled in the Prescribe review.
../../../docs/context/decision_log.md:864:  2. **Entry:** the terms line stays during Verifying / Checking so Verify & sign in never moves (amends D-44 for those two states); sign-in on a locked number goes to OTP in the locked state; cooldown line shows "Checking…" alone, boxes stay focused; one shared header spacing for OTP, offer and unlock so the fingerprint tile sits in the same place (D-61 pt 4 kept).
../../../docs/context/decision_log.md:875:  1. **Button icons by button type:** 56 px action buttons (18 px label) → 20 px icon; 48 px compact buttons (16 px label, e.g. View Rx) → 16 px; icon-only buttons (Back, Help, bell, Profile, close ×, viewer controls) → 20 px. Icons stay on the 16 / 20 / 24 scale; set centrally (RULES §9.1, beyond-salt). Rejected: 20 px on every button; icon = label size (an 18 px off-scale value); bigger labels to fit the icon scale.
../../../docs/context/decision_log.md:880:  6. **Consistency audit** (`CONSISTENCY-AUDIT.md`, 52 findings): all bugs and the recommended answers applied — card-to-card gap 16 on case / Prescribe; one logo lockup size 166 px, top 16; busy states keep the bar's height (Transferring keeps a greyed secondary row); OTP terms centred, "Terms & Conditions" on one line; OTP Verify never moves for one-line messages (reserved line under the boxes; notice-box states may move it); back / ✕ glyph on the 16 edge with the title after it in every header (B-07); text keyboard for notes; dose headings keep their form's unit ("Dose (ml)", "Dose (puffs)", injection "Dose" per D-15); Skip HA reason wording per D-70; duration chips at the label edge (D-55 kept).
../../../docs/context/decision_log.md:891:  3. **After a valid call only the confirm button:** 8a Confirm prescription; 8b Confirm & forward · Skip HA; 12 Confirm & transfer · Skip HA; 16 Confirm & forward · Skip HA (no Callback, CW-A3). Call again after a valid call is a next-version idea, decided with call-log data (CW-C4).
../../../docs/context/decision_log.md:899:  11. **16 copy (CW-F3):** one doctor line for A and B, unchanged — in B the Health Advisor joins only after Confirm, so it already reads right.
../../../docs/context/decision_log.md:905:  1. **Copy rules v2** (`docs/reviews/2026-11-03-copy-audit/COPY-RULES.md`, 26 rules) are the standard for all app text. They were drafted from D-48 / D-65 / D-66 / D-77 / D-81 / D-83, checked against the Atlassian, Polaris, Apple HIG and Material writing guides, and revised after a Codex critique (`codex-report.md`). Pointer in `docs/feedback-rules.md` §11.
../../../docs/context/decision_log.md:917:  3. Skip HA on 16 is unchanged (call already over → reason → Confirm prescription → 10a).
../../../docs/context/decision_log.md:973:- **Decision (Apurva):** after step 1, all 148 approved pictures are re-rendered from their approved sources on the new Mac, and screen captures are made repeatable. Each picture is checked to differ from the old one only by text-edge smoothing: no moved boxes, shifted rows or colour changes. The main thread reviews that evidence before the pictures replace the approved set. Then the anti-aliasing allow-list is removed, so app-vs-picture compares must match exactly, apart from listed, reasoned regions.
../../../docs/context/decision_log.md:988:- **Decision (Apurva):** the desktop preview frame is **390 : 844** (exactly 390 × 844 when the window allows, scaled down evenly otherwise), replacing 9:16 in the central design system (`design-system/RULES.md` §7, all projects). Review controls sit in **one column on the right**, top-aligned with the frame. "Test on phone" becomes the first folding row of the review panel (it was a separate card in the left gutter, session 4). Also: the QR / play link uses the Mac's network address when served locally, the default story is the happy path (patient answers, call over the gate), panel summaries wrap instead of being cut off, the **test numbers and codes** (app-logic §11) are listed in the Sign-in answers row (tap to fill), and "Settings" becomes **"Timings and limits"** in plain words with a Rule / Stand-in tag, moved with Event log under "Advanced" at the bottom.
../../../docs/context/decision_log.md:989:- **Why:** the approved pictures are 390 × 844 (and 360 wide). The 9:16 frame was about 22% shorter for its width than a modern phone, and up to 450 px wide on big screens, so the prototype showed squashed screens that didn't match what was approved. The panel and the QR card were on opposite sides and didn't line up with the frame. The typed test inputs were invisible in the panel, and "Settings · 26 values" meant nothing to a reviewer. Screens are designed by width (RULES §8) and already pass at 360 × 640 to 430, so no screen or picture changes.
../../../docs/context/decision_log.md:990:- **Rejected:** keeping 9:16 (doesn't match the approved pictures or real phones); a fixed 390 × 844 frame that doesn't scale (it would overflow short windows); the QR card in the left gutter (splits the controls).
../../../docs/context/decision_log.md:994:- **Main thread rulings (bugs, fixed where they occur):** red in the kit means only a typed size, colour or word (layout keywords and zeros are shown, not flagged); the kit excludes the reference page's own review and capture scaffolding (H05); the notice sits 16 below the field as the approved pictures show, and RULES §8.3 wording is corrected; the busy spinner ring uses `--tm-content-inverse` instead of `#fff` (same white); RULES §8.13's stale "Sign-in is 174 today" line is removed; the native logo ships as PNG exports of the locked SVG (no redraw); the static font files from the font's upstream repository at the commit Google Fonts pins are accepted.
../../../docs/context/decision_log.md:998:- **Follow-ups (main thread, after REPORT-2):** busy-spinner timing gets its token in the D-99 pass (`--tm-duration-spinner`); the 8-line `build.py` / `build_native.py` change that reads the `size` section is accepted; `.tm-btn--busy span > .tm-spinner { vertical-align: -3px }` stays as a `raw-ok` optical nudge; `feedback-state-map.md` placement rule now says 16 below the field / 8 below the button; one more fresh-AI check (Codex only) after D-99 for a strict pass.
../../../docs/context/decision_log.md:1011:- **Decision (Apurva, on the main thread's recommendations):** (o04) more than 10 digits that aren't a +91 / 0 prefix → show "That’s more than 10 digits. Check the number." instead of cutting silently. (o05) no passive offline notice on Sign-in; the notice shows only after Send OTP. (o07) the logo's 16 from the top is measured from the **safe area** (below the status bar / notch). (o08) Android back on Sign-in (the first screen) **leaves the app**. (o10) coming back from OTP via Change keeps the number and it edits normally (the first typed digit does **not** replace it). (o11) Terms → `https://www.truemeds.in/legal/terms-and-conditions`, Privacy → `https://www.truemeds.in/legal/privacy-policy` (placeholders, linked from the live Terms page), configurable from the server, not typed into the app. (o17) Sign up opens a browser **inside the app** (with a close button). (o18) nothing is remembered per number; an earlier answer shows again only after a new Send OTP. (o25) "New to Truemeds? Sign up" becomes one copy entry with a `{link}` placeholder. (o26) "Call Doctor Ops" on a device that can't call → open WhatsApp to the same number; without WhatsApp, show the number with a copy button.
../../../docs/context/decision_log.md:1012:- **Amended same day (Apurva):** the kit is a hand-off of a **prototype with a fake backend**, so the Backend and Design items (o01, o02, o03, o12, o15, o16, o19, o21, o22, o24) are not left open either: each becomes DECIDED with **the prototype's own mock value or behaviour**, marked `[MOCK]` and "keep configurable" so nobody treats it as a production promise. o23 (Expo or plain React Native, navigation library) is the app team's choice and is stated as theirs, not as an open question. o09 stays a prototype-only note.
../../../docs/context/decision_log.md:1032:- **Decision (Apurva):** returning unlock drops "Not you? Switch account". It keeps **Unlock** (primary) and **Use OTP instead** (quiet). Use OTP instead, and the automatic fallback after 3 failed unlocks, open **Sign-in with the remembered number filled in** — no SMS until the doctor taps Send OTP. To change account, the doctor edits the number there. Sign-in reached this way follows the normal Sign-in rules: no Back button; the phone's back gesture leaves the app (D-101); reopening the app shows unlock again. Amends D-61 point 3.

